{"id": "EUVD-2026-55540", "enisaUuid": "fbf0b4e0-d3f0-3b39-af09-74efcc5d0330", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlibceph: reject zero bucket types in crush_decode\n\nCRUSH bucket type 0 is reserved for devices.  The mapper relies on\nthat invariant and uses type 0 to identify leaf devices.\n\nIf crush_decode() accepts a bucket with type 0, a malformed CRUSH map\ncan make the mapper treat a negative bucket ID as a device and pass it\nto is_out(), which then indexes the OSD weight array with a negative\nvalue.\n\nReject zero bucket types while decoding the CRUSH map so the invalid\nstate never reaches the mapper.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:59:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:54", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/952ca5dc99913d169263f59fd689f586729a13c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/146461f09565afe3665e65b0423d3d6b0fe806c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80fc40e11cda1b5d990a3f69c6efa344fb5cd987", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8a9fb6bf806f9c4891e71ae1beab0c07c23a877", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/826cd1de5802fd392922785f9b64d76e65d2a100", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b2f1937f5fce8b7dd5432e7693e3cc8b5eece56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70998f91030ee083ecb336a1dff0701c20a38081", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05f90284223381005d6bcddab3fda4a97f9c3401"], "aliases": ["GHSA-33w3-5969-wxfc", "CVE-2026-68154"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04d2a9df-f558-34af-813a-058e3e0cc603", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f24e9980eb860d8600cbe5ef3d2fd9295320d229 <70998f91030ee083ecb336a1dff0701c20a38081"}, {"id": "08630422-afde-39f9-8c08-aa950b191d2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f24e9980eb860d8600cbe5ef3d2fd9295320d229 <05f90284223381005d6bcdda